    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To solve the expression $23^2 + 2(23)(2) + 2^2$, we will break it down and calculate each term step by step.\n\n1. Calculate $23^2$:\n\\[\n23^2 = 23 \\times 23 = 529\n\\]\n\n2. Calculate $2(23)(2)$:\n\\[\n2(23)(2) = 2 \\times 23 \\times 2 = 46\n\\]\n\n3. Calculate $2^2$:\n\\[\n2^2 = 2 \\times 2 = 4\n\\]\n\nNow, we will add these three results together:\n\\[\n529 + 46 + 4\n\\]\n\nFirst, add $529$ and $46$:\n\\[\n529 + 46 = 575\n\\]\n\nNext, add the result to $4$:\n\\[\n575 + 4 = 579\n\\]\n\nSo, the value of $23^2 + 2(23)(2) + 2^2$ is \\(\\boxed{579}\\).",
