    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To solve the expression \\(23^2 + 2(23)(2) + 2^2\\), we will break it down step by step and use the properties of exponents and arithmetic.\n\n1. **Square the first term:**\n   \\[\n   23^2 = 529\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply the second term:**\n   \\[\n   2(23)(2) = 4 \\times 23 = 92\n   \\]\n\n3. **Square the third term:**\n   \\[\n   2^2 = 4\n   \\]\n\nNow, we need to combine these results:\n\\[\n23^2 + 2(23)(2) + 2^2 = 529 + 92 + 4\n\\]\n\nNext, we add the numbers together:\n\\[\n529 + 92 = 621\n\\]\n\\[\n621 + 4 = 625\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of the expression is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{625}\n\\]",
